,[26212,18.3,2012,46,100,25],[26510,17.0,2012,49,106,25],[26511,17.5,2012,47,107,26],[26512,18.6,2012,46,107,25]],"links":[["Garden County in the Farmland Atlas","/farmland-atlas/nebraska/garden-county"],["ARC or PLC in Garden County","/arc-plc/nebraska/garden-county"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record here runs 75 years, 1951 to 2025, on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 17 grids. February to March and November to December each came in under 90% of normal in 38 of those years. In 2025, November to December finished at 27% of normal on the middle, and so far in 2026 February to March sits at 23%. May to June is the wettest pair with a normal of 6.26 inches and January to February the driest at 0.76 inches.</p>"}
